-- title:
--   Vertex-fixing group elements have trivial Drinfeld period
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $K_0$, let $\varpi \in R$ be irreducible, and assume the residue ring $R/(\varpi)$ is finite. Let $K$ be a complete, algebraically closed extension field of $K_0$ carrying a valuation $v$ with values in a linearly ordered commutative group with zero $\Gamma_0$, subject to: every element of $R$ has $v \le 1$ in $K$; conversely every $a \in K_0$ with $v(a) \le 1$ lies in the image of $R$; the powers $v(\varpi)^N$ are cofinal towards $0$ in $\Gamma_0$; and for all $x,y \in K$ with $v(x) < 1$ and $y \ne 0$ some power $v(x)^n \le v(y)$ (a rank-one condition). Let $\varpi_1$ be a pseudo-uniformiser, i.e. an element of $K_0$ with $0 < v(\varpi_1) < 1$ whose powers bracket the valuation of every nonzero element of $K_0$, and assume `IsExhausted`: every point of the Drinfeld upper half plane $\Omega = K \setminus \operatorname{im}(K_0 \to K)$ lies in one of the affinoids $\mathrm{affinoid}\ \varpi_1\ n$. Let $G$ be a group with a homomorphism $\rho : G \to \mathrm{PGL}_2(K_0)$ and an action on the vertices of the Bruhat–Tits tree of $R$ (homothety classes of full lattices in $K_0^2$, adjacency generated by the lattice-adjacency relation) which preserves adjacency, which agrees with the action through $\rho$ (`ActsThrough`), and all of whose vertex stabilisers are finite. Let $\tau$ be a $G$-invariant two-colouring of the vertices taking distinct values on adjacent vertices, let $E$ be a finite type together with a bijection onto the set of $G$-orbits of darts whose chosen representative has source of colour $0$, and let $g_0, g_a \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, $w_0, w_a \in \mathrm{affinoid}\ \varpi_1\ 0$ (so $v(w) \le 1$ and $v(w - a) \ge 1$ for every $a \in K_0$ with $v(a) \le 1$), with the colours of $g_0 \cdot \mathrm{stdVertex}$ and $g_a \cdot \mathrm{stdVertex}$ distinct. Then for every $\alpha \in G$ fixing some vertex $v_1$ and every $\beta \in G$, the period $\Theta(a, \rho(\alpha) a; z_0; \rho(\beta) z_0)$ equals $1$, where $a$ and $z_0$ are the images of $w_a$ and $w_0$ under the Möbius actions of $g_a$ and $g_0$ respectively.
--
--   This is the statement that the Manin–Drinfeld period pairing attached to a tree lattice $\rho$ with finite vertex stabilisers is trivial on elements fixing a vertex, so that it kills the subgroup of $G^{\mathrm{ab}}$ generated by the vertex stabilisers. It is used in the construction of the period datum of a Mumford quotient, in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_periodDatum_Q_mul_period_eq_one_of_mumfordQuotient`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_periodDatum_Q_mul_period_eq_one_of_mumfordQuotient), where the pairing must descend to the cycle lattice of the quotient graph.
